Rule 3 (If one of the inputs is complex, the other one should be complex as well)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11 then dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11 else if dtype_(v_2) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 11 then dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 4 (If input tensor dtype is bool, the other tensor should be bool as well)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then dtype_(v_2) = 0
>>
Rule 5 (If one tensor has zero dimensions, the other tensor must have zero dimensions too)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0 then ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, j) = 0
>>
Rule 6 (If the input tensor is a scalar, the other tensor must be broadcastable to scalar or be a scalar itself.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ (ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1))
>>
Rule 7 (The result type can't be cast to the desired output type)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 8 (input tensor must be bool)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0
