Rule 12 (When the input tensor is not a scalar, at least one of the dimensions must be greater than 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≠ 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1
>>
Rule 13 (When multiplying a tensor by a scalar, if the tensor has one or more dimensions where its size is zero, the scalar value should be zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0 then v_2 = 0
>>
